From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 00:24:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tests/dx11_cube: real PeekMessage loop + atomic-write traces
 + bitmap-font overlay
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WndProc now logs WM_MOUSEMOVE/DOWN/UP via WriteFile(STD_ERROR_HANDLE) — single
syscall keeps lines coherent even when sharing fd 2 with ntdll's per-syscall
trace channel on iOS. Adds an in-frame text overlay rendering the latest mouse
event line in top-left via the cube's existing pipeline (identity MVP + depth
disabled + a 5x7 bitmap font). Used to validate end-to-end input on iOS:
UIKit touches → winios.drv → wineserver → cube WndProc.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Madeira-commit: c3e8451feb8f87c0b84c2f78f377ec109078bed1
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-dxmt-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
